WEBVTT

00:02.878 --> 00:05.005
[grunting]

00:07.966 --> 00:10.052
[thwacking]

00:22.105 --> 00:23.273
What a dummy.

00:24.525 --> 00:27.069
[exhaling]

00:29.071 --> 00:31.323
Oh, Master.

00:31.406 --> 00:34.618
[Nagakura]
At it again, training so early?

00:36.078 --> 00:38.580
My apologies.
Did I wake you?

00:38.664 --> 00:39.748
Nah.

00:42.543 --> 00:46.088
Don't overdo it.
Your hands are all torn up.

00:47.798 --> 00:49.091
[sighs]

00:50.884 --> 00:52.302
[Sasaki] Master.
[Nagakura] Hm?

00:52.386 --> 00:54.179
I'm sorry to impose, but...

00:58.016 --> 01:00.435
I'd be grateful
for your instruction.

01:03.063 --> 01:05.107
What are you talking about?

01:05.190 --> 01:07.150
You're plenty strong already.

01:07.234 --> 01:09.027
There's nothing more
I can teach you.

01:09.111 --> 01:10.028
[exclaims softly]

01:10.112 --> 01:13.240
[♪♪♪]

01:13.323 --> 01:17.119
You're the only master I'll
ever have, Nagakura Shinpachi.

01:17.202 --> 01:19.079
Cut it out.
Spare me the flattery.

01:19.162 --> 01:21.248
It's not flattery.

01:21.331 --> 01:23.542
You accepted your own
lack of natural talent

01:23.625 --> 01:26.420
and overcame it with nothing
but pure hard work.

01:26.503 --> 01:28.672
The way you became
this strong...

01:28.755 --> 01:30.841
you're my inspiration, Master.

01:30.924 --> 01:32.259
[scoffs]

01:32.342 --> 01:35.512
No talent, no talent...
You've got some nerve.

01:35.554 --> 01:37.681
I can't tell
if you're complimenting me

01:37.764 --> 01:39.515
or insulting me.

01:39.600 --> 01:40.726
My apologies.

01:42.185 --> 01:45.229
Whatever.
It's the truth, anyway.

01:51.445 --> 01:52.404
[grunts]

01:55.574 --> 01:58.035
You've gotten good
at that disarming technique.

01:58.076 --> 01:59.661
All thanks to you, Master.

02:06.043 --> 02:07.169
Bring it.

02:08.461 --> 02:10.922
This "talentless" senior
will give you a lesson.

02:12.257 --> 02:13.508
Thank you very much.

02:20.557 --> 02:23.518
[insects chirring]

02:39.242 --> 02:42.245
Half past six. I'll be
waiting at Shinkenji Temple.

02:50.170 --> 02:51.254
Guess who?

02:51.338 --> 02:52.881
[sword slices]
[blood spilling]

02:58.762 --> 03:00.347
[grunts]

03:05.435 --> 03:06.687
[coughs]

03:08.855 --> 03:10.774
THE CORPS CODE

03:10.816 --> 03:12.442
[yelling]

03:12.526 --> 03:15.278
[grunting]
[blows landing]

03:23.954 --> 03:26.289
[coughs]

03:26.373 --> 03:28.375
Come on, Shimada.
What's the matter?

03:30.335 --> 03:32.003
Put more spirit into it.

03:32.087 --> 03:35.340
[gasping]
My apologies, Vice-Commander.

03:36.633 --> 03:39.010
[Okita]
Hijikata doesn't hold back.

03:39.094 --> 03:42.514
[Kondo]
Face every opponent
with everything you've got.

03:42.597 --> 03:45.767
It's the only way to show
true respect for your opponent.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.608
[grunting]

03:53.692 --> 03:56.236
[♪♪♪]

03:59.156 --> 04:00.657
[groans]

04:02.659 --> 04:03.952
[groaning]

04:14.212 --> 04:15.797
[Okita]
But they are all intimidated.

04:15.881 --> 04:17.673
[student 1]
He's just too damn strong.

04:17.757 --> 04:20.260
[student 2]
He's making Shimada
look like a child...

04:22.763 --> 04:23.764
Out of the way!

04:23.847 --> 04:25.390
[Hijikata]
Heisuke, we're practicing.

04:25.474 --> 04:28.894
This is no time for that!

04:30.437 --> 04:34.274
Aijiro...
Aijiro has been killed!

04:40.197 --> 04:42.365
[indistinct chatter]

04:42.449 --> 04:44.451
[doshin]
Back off.

04:45.368 --> 04:47.245
Back off. Come on.

04:47.329 --> 04:50.457
[♪♪♪]

04:50.540 --> 04:51.457
Hey!

04:56.755 --> 04:58.590
[crowd exclaiming]

05:10.435 --> 05:17.609
SONG OF THE SAMURAI

05:25.116 --> 05:26.701
Are you sure it was Aijiro?

05:28.662 --> 05:29.621
Yes.

05:31.373 --> 05:32.749
According to
the magistrate's office,

05:32.832 --> 05:34.543
the body had countless
sword wounds.

05:35.919 --> 05:37.254
They said the fatal wound

05:37.295 --> 05:39.548
was being run through
from back to stomach.

05:43.218 --> 05:44.511
Does Shinpachi know?

05:47.806 --> 05:48.723
No idea.

05:49.933 --> 05:53.478
Haven't seen Nagakura
at the dojo today.

05:54.479 --> 05:56.940
Any idea who did it?

05:57.023 --> 05:58.608
No idea.

05:58.650 --> 06:02.404
The magistrate's office thinks
it was probably a robber

06:02.487 --> 06:04.281
since his belongings were taken.

06:04.322 --> 06:06.283
A robber?

06:06.324 --> 06:08.702
No way he'd be killed
by a common thief.

06:10.579 --> 06:13.081
[footsteps approaching]

06:15.458 --> 06:16.626
[Niimi]
Coming in.

06:20.505 --> 06:22.507
What do you want, Niimi?

06:24.467 --> 06:26.720
I hear one of your men
got himself killed.

06:28.513 --> 06:30.432
I see you get news quickly.

06:31.516 --> 06:33.810
Our faction's full of new blood,
you see.

06:33.852 --> 06:37.647
Can't have them losing morale
over something trivial.

06:39.107 --> 06:40.567
Trivial?

06:41.443 --> 06:43.528
The way he died.

06:45.238 --> 06:46.489
Get it right.

06:48.325 --> 06:49.743
His name was Sasaki Aijiro.

06:49.826 --> 06:51.119
Ah?

06:51.202 --> 06:52.495
There is no one in this corps

06:52.537 --> 06:54.289
named "the guy who got killed."

06:54.372 --> 06:57.626
[scoffs]
Killed by a common thief,
I hear.

06:59.169 --> 07:02.464
A weakling like that isn't even
worth learning the name of.

07:02.547 --> 07:04.174
You bastard...

07:04.257 --> 07:06.718
How dare you insult
a fallen comrade?

07:06.801 --> 07:08.470
One...

07:08.553 --> 07:11.056
If you fail to kill
and take a wound to your back,

07:11.139 --> 07:12.432
it is seppuku.

07:16.811 --> 07:20.190
This Sasaki...
whatever his name was...

07:20.273 --> 07:23.443
was cut down
while turning his back.

07:25.278 --> 07:28.657
He'd have had to commit seppuku
even if he had survived.

07:31.451 --> 07:33.078
That's the Corps Code, isn't it?

07:34.913 --> 07:36.623
Kondo.

07:36.706 --> 07:41.294
One of your men has disgraced
the name of the Mibu Roshigumi.

07:41.378 --> 07:43.880
How are you going to answer
for this?

07:43.922 --> 07:45.382
Hey, Niimi.

07:45.465 --> 07:46.716
[Nagakura]
Stop, Toshi.

07:48.343 --> 07:49.469
Shinpachi.

07:51.096 --> 07:53.014
What he's saying is bullshit.

07:54.557 --> 07:56.351
There's no way Aijiro
would turn his back

07:56.433 --> 07:57.602
on some common thief.

08:00.563 --> 08:05.944
In that case...
who do you claim did it?

08:06.027 --> 08:10.740
I don't know,
but I'll find whoever it is.

08:12.450 --> 08:13.785
I'll find the bastard...

08:15.495 --> 08:16.997
and finish them.

08:33.638 --> 08:38.518
THE CORPS CODE

08:38.601 --> 08:41.520
ONE, IF YOU FAIL TO KILL
AND TAKE A WOUND TO YOUR BACK,

08:41.604 --> 08:42.938
IT IS SEPPUKU

08:47.318 --> 08:48.653
[sighs]

09:03.334 --> 09:06.212
[screams]

09:15.346 --> 09:17.223
[footsteps approaching]

09:17.307 --> 09:19.726
[Seiki]
What's up? Bye.

09:42.123 --> 09:45.043
[♪♪♪]

09:52.675 --> 09:56.054
Couldn't resist
causing some trouble, huh?

09:57.514 --> 09:59.182
You think I overdid it?

10:00.892 --> 10:05.313
There's nothing like picking
on the weak, is there?

10:05.396 --> 10:08.108
I just get so into it.
Ha-ha!

10:08.191 --> 10:09.234
Whatever.

10:10.527 --> 10:11.569
[coin clinks]

10:11.653 --> 10:14.030
Whoa, damn.

10:14.072 --> 10:17.117
Are you sure I should get
this much for that little thing?

10:20.537 --> 10:22.288
But are you sure about this?

10:23.915 --> 10:26.709
The truth is, I was ordered
to assassinate Kondo Isami

10:26.793 --> 10:28.753
so I went undercover with them.

10:28.837 --> 10:30.922
That's not your place
to worry about.

10:32.549 --> 10:33.800
Right.

10:36.427 --> 10:38.263
So, what's next?

10:39.722 --> 10:41.099
You've done enough.

10:41.182 --> 10:42.350
[laughing]

10:42.433 --> 10:44.018
For real?

10:44.102 --> 10:47.230
You think taking out one grunt
is enough to bring down Kondo?

10:47.313 --> 10:49.023
Ah.

10:51.234 --> 10:54.154
You're a true strategist, Niimi.
Just what I'd expect.

10:55.488 --> 10:59.075
Guess I'll use this cash
to celebrate.

10:59.159 --> 11:00.118
Surely.

11:02.579 --> 11:04.289
You didn't mess up?

11:04.372 --> 11:06.791
Of course not.

11:20.180 --> 11:22.765
You were listening,
weren't you, Yamazaki?

11:25.059 --> 11:31.399
Money, money, money!
Money! Money!

11:31.482 --> 11:33.443
Keep an eye on him.

11:33.484 --> 11:34.444
Yes.

11:49.000 --> 11:50.877
Move.

11:50.960 --> 11:51.878
Welcome.

11:53.087 --> 11:54.005
Hey.

11:56.090 --> 12:00.678
Skipping patrol to go drinking?
Must be nice.

12:00.762 --> 12:04.766
Crap. I got busted.
[chuckles]

12:04.849 --> 12:06.392
And you're not even wearing
your damn coat.

12:09.187 --> 12:10.647
You're not taking this
seriously?

12:10.730 --> 12:13.691
[laughs]
No, no, no, of course I am!

12:13.775 --> 12:16.527
Nagakura, you came
all the way out here...

12:16.611 --> 12:18.363
So aren't you slacking off too?

12:20.031 --> 12:22.200
Won't you have a drink with me?

12:23.534 --> 12:24.869
Forget that. Saeki...

12:27.413 --> 12:28.498
It's about Aijiro.

12:29.540 --> 12:31.125
[laughing]

12:31.209 --> 12:33.878
Heard he got killed
by some thugs, right?

12:37.715 --> 12:38.675
Here.

12:38.716 --> 12:41.010
[chuckles]
Thanks.

12:43.388 --> 12:44.931
I saw his body.

12:46.808 --> 12:51.062
The fatal blow
one strike from back to stomach.

12:52.897 --> 12:55.400
The style of the sword strike
was Shindo Munen-ryu.

12:56.943 --> 12:58.528
That's your style too, isn't it?

12:58.569 --> 13:00.280
[drink continues pouring]

13:01.781 --> 13:03.908
What's more, you're from Choshu.

13:09.872 --> 13:13.293
What a waste!

13:17.588 --> 13:19.257
You're the one
who killed Aijiro.

13:23.219 --> 13:26.222
[laughing]
Whoa, what is this
all of a sudden?

13:26.306 --> 13:29.434
Why would I go and kill
one of our own comrades?

13:29.517 --> 13:31.894
Besides, there must be
a thousand swordsmen in Kyo

13:31.978 --> 13:33.354
who use that style.

13:34.230 --> 13:36.733
Including you, right, Nagakura?

13:36.774 --> 13:39.027
Anyway, I already deserted
the Choshu clan.

13:40.820 --> 13:42.739
What happened to your finger?

13:42.822 --> 13:44.449
Ah... Ha-ha.

13:46.159 --> 13:49.078
A girl bit me over
in the pleasure district.

13:49.162 --> 13:51.914
You'd wear a splint for just
a little bite on your pinky?

13:53.665 --> 13:56.836
Aijiro broke it with his
disarming technique, didn't he?

14:00.757 --> 14:01.883
Don't move.

14:06.888 --> 14:08.890
You plan to fight
with that hand?

14:15.480 --> 14:17.190
[sighing]
Ah...

14:22.278 --> 14:23.404
[laughing]

14:23.488 --> 14:26.866
[♪♪♪]

14:36.709 --> 14:38.127
[grunting]

14:38.169 --> 14:40.171
[laughing]

14:53.059 --> 14:54.977
Aah!
Oh-ho-ho-ho!

15:00.233 --> 15:02.110
[laughing]

15:05.321 --> 15:08.032
Even you could see
the huge gap between us, right?

15:09.367 --> 15:10.952
You know...

15:11.035 --> 15:14.163
you're going to get crushed,
so why aren't you running?

15:15.498 --> 15:19.627
So, master and student
are alike, huh? Hilarious.

15:21.504 --> 15:24.757
Let me ask you instead.

15:24.841 --> 15:26.134
Huh?

15:28.386 --> 15:30.263
There's one thing
I just don't get.

15:34.434 --> 15:37.270
Why did you have to kill Aijiro
in such a brutal way?

15:39.564 --> 15:41.065
A man with your skill...

15:42.984 --> 15:45.528
you could have finished him off
in a single blow.

15:45.570 --> 15:48.197
[laughing]

15:48.281 --> 15:51.367
I guess a hack like you
wouldn't get it.

15:53.911 --> 15:55.997
Killing someone
in a crushing win....

15:58.415 --> 16:01.210
feels better
than screwing a woman.

16:01.294 --> 16:02.879
[laughing]

16:02.920 --> 16:05.214
You bastard!

16:12.930 --> 16:14.265
[gasps playfully]

16:16.267 --> 16:17.977
What the hell is that?

16:18.060 --> 16:19.729
Trying to make me die
of laughter?

16:19.770 --> 16:21.439
[laughing]

16:28.696 --> 16:30.448
Don't you mock me!

16:33.493 --> 16:35.077
[yelling fiercely]

16:43.461 --> 16:46.214
And there it is.
A decisive victory.

16:50.134 --> 16:52.220
Now this feels good.

16:55.806 --> 16:57.308
Way too easy.

17:00.520 --> 17:02.146
[grunting]

17:07.026 --> 17:09.194
I can't hold it in anymore.

17:16.827 --> 17:18.246
Sorry, but here I come!

17:25.502 --> 17:26.628
[exclaims]

17:29.298 --> 17:30.675
[flesh squelches]
[chokes]

17:34.262 --> 17:36.514
You know, Saeki...

17:36.597 --> 17:38.516
the real thrill comes...

17:40.059 --> 17:46.232
when you crush someone
far beyond your own skill.

17:49.026 --> 17:50.444
[coughing]

17:53.072 --> 17:55.533
W-Wait! Nagakura, please!

17:57.368 --> 18:00.955
Do you have any proof that
I'm the one who killed Aijiro?

18:01.038 --> 18:02.540
Y-You don't have any, do you?

18:02.623 --> 18:04.709
I'm not sloppy
with things like that.

18:06.210 --> 18:08.004
I-If you finish me off now

18:08.087 --> 18:09.797
the truth about me
being the killer

18:09.880 --> 18:11.299
will just be swept
under the rug.

18:11.382 --> 18:14.343
S-S-So, look! I'll cooperate!

18:14.385 --> 18:16.721
I'll go to the magistrate's
office... anywhere you say.

18:19.056 --> 18:20.474
[crying]

18:20.558 --> 18:24.103
I'll tell you everything I know,
I swear.

18:28.899 --> 18:33.654
Please! Just spare my life!

18:42.413 --> 18:43.331
I see.

18:44.874 --> 18:45.791
Fine.

18:49.253 --> 18:50.463
[sniveling]
Thank you!

18:51.339 --> 18:54.634
Thank you so much.

18:56.052 --> 18:59.263
I'll be in your debt
for the rest of my life.

19:03.559 --> 19:04.518
[blade rings]

19:05.603 --> 19:06.520
Oh?

19:07.563 --> 19:08.564
[blade clatters]

19:11.108 --> 19:13.736
You're such a transparent
piece of shit.

19:13.778 --> 19:16.447
[gasping]

19:18.532 --> 19:19.617
[neck snaps]

19:31.170 --> 19:34.298
[♪♪♪]

19:52.942 --> 19:54.735
[Niimi]
So, Nagakura made his move.

19:56.278 --> 19:57.405
[Yamazaki]
Yes.

19:59.240 --> 20:00.366
Just as I predicted.

20:02.118 --> 20:03.369
The winner is...

20:05.246 --> 20:06.664
Nagakura Shinpachi.

20:08.833 --> 20:10.334
I see.

20:11.961 --> 20:14.422
Saeki was a fool.

20:14.463 --> 20:19.343
For all his talent with a sword,
he let his skill go to his head.

20:22.555 --> 20:24.598
[chuckles]

20:24.682 --> 20:29.145
And with this...
Kondo Isami is finished.

20:29.228 --> 20:33.357
[♪♪♪]

20:48.706 --> 20:50.583
There are no sword wounds
on him.

20:52.793 --> 20:54.378
Unbelievable...

20:55.629 --> 20:58.424
Nagakura...
You beat the best dual-wielder

20:58.507 --> 21:00.092
with just brute force.

21:00.176 --> 21:05.264
Hey. Hey, Shinpachi! Hey, why?

21:06.390 --> 21:08.517
Why'd you try to shoulder this
all alone?

21:08.559 --> 21:12.021
Toshi, what's the problem?

21:12.062 --> 21:15.107
You guys, that scumbag Saeki
is the one who killed Aijiro!

21:15.191 --> 21:17.401
This was righteous revenge!
Right?!

21:18.652 --> 21:19.612
Answer me!

21:21.530 --> 21:23.949
If only there were proof
of that.

21:39.965 --> 21:42.468
Kondo, any luck?

21:42.551 --> 21:45.387
I searched Saeki's belongings

21:45.429 --> 21:49.225
but found no proof
that he killed Sasaki Aijiro.

21:49.308 --> 21:51.477
Hey!
Did you check properly, boss?

21:52.728 --> 21:53.646
Yes.

21:55.147 --> 21:56.398
Nagakura...

21:57.650 --> 21:59.652
why did you pass judgment
on Saeki?

22:01.612 --> 22:03.614
If you passed judgment
on an assumption

22:03.697 --> 22:06.242
then this is
just a private duel

22:06.325 --> 22:08.911
fought for your own
selfish reasons.

22:08.953 --> 22:13.040
Don't tell me
you've forgotten the Corps Code?

22:14.291 --> 22:16.001
One.

22:16.085 --> 22:18.754
Do not engage
in personal fights.

22:18.838 --> 22:21.757
Anyone who violates these
articles must commit seppuku.

22:26.512 --> 22:27.888
I am prepared for that.

22:32.852 --> 22:36.939
[♪♪♪]

22:37.022 --> 22:40.150
Hold on a second!
What do you mean, prepared?!

22:42.987 --> 22:43.946
Hey, Shinpachi!

22:46.782 --> 22:48.492
How did you know
it was Saeki?

22:50.369 --> 22:51.787
At least answer that much.

22:55.666 --> 22:56.625
Everyone...

22:59.670 --> 23:01.380
I'm sorry
for all the trouble.

23:04.383 --> 23:05.551
Hey, Shinpachi...

23:07.261 --> 23:08.637
But I have no regrets.

23:19.940 --> 23:21.817
Knock it off!

23:26.572 --> 23:30.701
[♪♪♪]

23:41.211 --> 23:42.254
Farewell.

23:42.338 --> 23:43.547
Shinpachi!

23:44.882 --> 23:46.133
[wakizashi clatters]

23:49.303 --> 23:50.638
Shinpachi.

23:52.723 --> 23:55.684
You're not meant to fall
in a place like this.

24:00.314 --> 24:01.440
Boss...

24:19.375 --> 24:20.542
Niimi!

24:22.836 --> 24:27.591
I ask that you grant a brief
stay of Shinpachi's seppuku.

24:29.885 --> 24:31.345
[Okita]
Kondo, please stop!

24:31.428 --> 24:32.471
I beg of you!

24:32.554 --> 24:34.014
[Hijikata]
Hey!

24:35.265 --> 24:36.725
[Niimi]
Oh?

24:36.767 --> 24:40.479
So, the Commander himself
would bend the Corps Code.

24:41.772 --> 24:44.024
And you expect to maintain
discipline that way?

24:46.819 --> 24:50.698
Shinpachi's failure is my own.

24:55.285 --> 24:56.620
In his place...

24:58.497 --> 25:00.416
I will resign my position
as Commander.

25:00.457 --> 25:03.002
What are you saying,
boss!

25:03.085 --> 25:04.128
As will I.

25:10.467 --> 25:12.386
I shall resign my post
as vice-commander.

25:12.469 --> 25:14.430
Yamanami...

25:14.471 --> 25:16.724
[laughing heartily]

25:18.267 --> 25:20.853
What is this farce?!

25:20.936 --> 25:24.982
As if that could ever be a fair
trade for Nagakura's seppuku.

25:25.065 --> 25:28.944
Then Nagakura's life
must be pretty damn cheap.

25:30.362 --> 25:31.321
Then...

25:35.075 --> 25:36.118
what do we need to do?

25:38.245 --> 25:39.246
Commit seppuku.

25:40.330 --> 25:42.332
Hey, you bastard! Cut it out!

25:42.416 --> 25:44.168
Who's being ridiculous here?

25:44.251 --> 25:48.172
Anyone who violates the Corps
Codes must commit seppuku!

25:49.548 --> 25:52.051
You're the ones
who made that rule!

25:53.761 --> 25:55.971
[Serizawa exclaiming slowly]

25:58.682 --> 26:00.726
This is a lively bunch.

26:03.520 --> 26:06.815
Niimi, come on,
cut them some slack.

26:06.857 --> 26:08.525
But...

26:08.609 --> 26:12.237
Besides, what's fun
in making them commit seppuku?

26:13.363 --> 26:14.823
[stammers]

26:22.706 --> 26:24.917
Kondo. Yamanami!

26:26.668 --> 26:28.921
You have Serizawa's mercy
to thank for this.

26:32.966 --> 26:36.553
Hey, Niimi. Watch your mouth.

26:36.637 --> 26:38.514
Why would
a Vice-Commander like me

26:38.597 --> 26:40.516
listen to
a rank-and-file soldier?

26:40.557 --> 26:42.226
You rotten country-samurai!

26:42.309 --> 26:46.855
From this moment on,
you're all just common soldiers.

26:46.939 --> 26:50.526
You will all serve
under Serizawa.

26:50.567 --> 26:52.653
That is the condition
for granting Nagakura

26:52.736 --> 26:54.029
a reprieve from seppuku.

26:55.697 --> 26:58.033
Is that acceptable, Serizawa?

27:00.661 --> 27:03.914
I don't care.
Do whatever you want.

27:20.764 --> 27:22.558
[shouts]
[punch thuds]

27:22.641 --> 27:24.101
What the hell are you doing!

27:30.691 --> 27:31.984
Yamanami, you too!

27:37.573 --> 27:40.409
[Niimi]
That was a surprise.

27:40.450 --> 27:42.536
I can't believe
you showed them mercy.

27:42.619 --> 27:44.246
[Serizawa]
Mercy, huh.

27:44.329 --> 27:47.583
[Niimi]
It was the best chance
to take out Kondo, wasn't it?

27:47.624 --> 27:50.794
I don't remember
showing any mercy.

27:51.795 --> 27:54.131
Eh?
Niimi...

27:55.883 --> 27:58.635
If you want to kill,
do it with your own hands.

27:58.719 --> 28:01.096
Seppuku is the most boring thing
in this world.

28:01.180 --> 28:02.806
[yawns]

28:03.724 --> 28:04.850
Serizawa!

28:07.311 --> 28:08.353
I heard the news.

28:09.646 --> 28:11.106
I heard you used the Corps Code

28:11.190 --> 28:12.941
to bring the Kondo faction
under our control.

28:12.983 --> 28:15.819
[chuckles]
That was all Niimi's doing.

28:17.696 --> 28:22.159
Well, well.
I'm impressed, Vice-Commander.

28:22.242 --> 28:24.578
Watch your mouth!

28:24.661 --> 28:26.663
I'm your superior officer.

28:26.747 --> 28:29.291
What example does that set
for our men?

28:29.374 --> 28:32.711
[scoffs]
That's ridiculous.
We're on the same side.

28:35.672 --> 28:38.091
Well, how about we go out

28:38.175 --> 28:40.636
and celebrate bringing the Kondo
faction under our wing?

28:40.677 --> 28:41.887
No.

28:43.722 --> 28:46.141
I think it's about time
for our little festival.

28:46.225 --> 28:48.393
[laughs]

28:48.477 --> 28:50.729
[♪♪♪]

28:50.812 --> 28:57.903
SEPTEMBER 24, 1863

29:23.720 --> 29:25.305
[Hirayama]
We are the Mibu Roshigumi!

29:25.347 --> 29:27.724
[stammering]
Hey, hey, hey!
What's all this about?

29:27.808 --> 29:30.852
[whimpering]

29:30.894 --> 29:33.730
This is an official inspection.

29:33.814 --> 29:35.649
You've cornered the market
on raw silk

29:35.732 --> 29:37.609
and kept all the profits
for yourselves!

29:37.693 --> 29:40.654
It's time you learned
how much suffering

29:40.737 --> 29:43.573
you've caused
the people of this city!

29:44.783 --> 29:45.909
Move out of the way.

29:49.579 --> 29:53.041
This money isn't for you
to line your own pockets with.

29:53.125 --> 29:55.252
It will be used
for the people of Kyo.

29:56.753 --> 29:57.754
Got it?

29:57.838 --> 29:59.464
[men whimpering]

29:59.548 --> 30:01.383
We'll be back.

30:01.466 --> 30:03.343
All right, let's move out.

30:03.427 --> 30:04.428
[soldiers]
Sir!

30:13.854 --> 30:15.981
Now... let's begin.

30:24.823 --> 30:25.907
[laughs]

30:25.991 --> 30:27.617
What are you doing,
Serizawa?

30:27.701 --> 30:29.453
Isn't it obvious?
It's a festival!

30:29.536 --> 30:32.622
Come on, you light one, too.

30:34.750 --> 30:36.084
Do it.

30:36.126 --> 30:38.754
Sir! Bring the fire, you lot!

30:38.837 --> 30:41.590
[men shouting indistinctly]

30:53.810 --> 30:57.356
You need more fire!
Go on! Keep going!

30:57.439 --> 30:58.982
[laughs]

30:59.066 --> 31:00.859
Burn it! Burn more!

31:08.867 --> 31:11.870
Serizawa! We're losing
our source of money!

31:11.953 --> 31:13.372
Look, Niimi.

31:16.166 --> 31:20.379
It just burns.
That's the beauty of it.

31:20.462 --> 31:24.132
[♪♪♪]

31:24.174 --> 31:26.009
For everything to burn...

31:27.928 --> 31:29.638
and turn to ashes.

32:02.379 --> 32:04.339
[laughing]

32:04.423 --> 32:08.552
Serizawa Kamo.
A man I must have.

32:10.345 --> 32:12.180
A moral compass
that points somewhere

32:12.222 --> 32:14.099
beyond good and evil,
profit and loss.

32:14.182 --> 32:17.602
One who has no interest
in money or honor...

32:17.686 --> 32:19.938
is a fascinating man indeed.

32:21.106 --> 32:24.860
Whether or not Serizawa Kamo
sides with us

32:24.901 --> 32:26.736
rests entirely
on your shoulders, Mr. Niimi.

32:26.820 --> 32:29.030
You needn't worry, Mr. Kusaka.

32:29.114 --> 32:32.033
He's just a simple-minded brute.

32:32.075 --> 32:35.245
He doesn't have a shred
of loyalty to the Shogunate.

32:36.580 --> 32:38.081
I'm counting on you.

32:39.124 --> 32:42.169
Our preparations
are all set as well.

32:42.252 --> 32:44.087
[Sanjo]
On this occasion...

32:44.171 --> 32:45.881
[Kusaka]
The day after your men attack

32:45.964 --> 32:47.257
and burn down the Yamato-ya...

32:48.550 --> 32:53.388
The Emperor has announced
he'll lead

32:53.472 --> 32:56.766
the expulsionist faction
in seizing power.

32:56.850 --> 32:58.894
So the signal
to overthrow the shogunate

32:58.935 --> 33:00.061
has finally been given.

33:00.145 --> 33:01.897
We must use this momentum

33:01.938 --> 33:07.652
to eliminate
Matsudaira Katamori!

33:09.070 --> 33:12.407
I'm counting on you, Niimi.

33:12.491 --> 33:15.076
How you drove Kondo Isami
into a corner

33:15.160 --> 33:17.913
the other day
was truly brilliant.

33:17.954 --> 33:21.166
I'll take care of Lord Katamori.

33:21.249 --> 33:24.336
150 Men in the Serizawa faction
are under my direct command.

33:25.587 --> 33:28.131
I can mobilize them
at a moment's notice.

33:28.965 --> 33:30.759
That's very reassuring.

33:38.183 --> 33:40.477
This is for you, Niimi.
Do as you like.

33:59.079 --> 34:03.500
[♪♪♪]

34:10.549 --> 34:12.425
[footsteps]

34:22.101 --> 34:26.188
[panting excitedly]

34:26.273 --> 34:30.068
Money. Money. Money! Money!

34:31.027 --> 34:32.612
You really love money that much?

34:32.654 --> 34:36.199
I do. It's the one thing
that will never betray me.

34:43.831 --> 34:44.873
Found it.

35:04.436 --> 35:08.231
Good, things
are really coming together!

35:10.066 --> 35:12.569
Oume, how about a song?

35:13.862 --> 35:15.113
Certainly.

35:21.411 --> 35:26.249
[Oume playing and singing]

35:34.049 --> 35:36.926
[playing and singing fade]

35:42.932 --> 35:44.059
Serizawa.

35:44.100 --> 35:48.188
[♪♪♪]

35:48.271 --> 35:49.439
What's this?

35:57.864 --> 35:59.908
[loud shouting]

35:59.949 --> 36:03.411
[Todo, chuckling]
You are so loud.
Come on! Bring it on!

36:22.972 --> 36:25.392
[laughs]

36:27.977 --> 36:29.938
Hey, Shimada!

36:29.979 --> 36:32.691
How many times
do I have to tell you?

36:32.774 --> 36:36.611
Don't you have any damn respect
for your seniors?!

36:36.695 --> 36:41.157
My apologies. I'll be sure
to go easy on you next time.

36:41.241 --> 36:42.325
Are you mocking me?!

36:42.409 --> 36:45.328
Hey, you are getting
all worked up.

36:46.162 --> 36:47.455
I mean...

36:47.539 --> 36:49.290
Yeah, I can see
why you're pissed.

36:49.374 --> 36:51.584
You two are the only ones
even training.

36:54.254 --> 36:56.756
Everyone's been sucked
into the Serizawa faction

36:58.508 --> 37:01.136
and now it's just us left
in the Kondo faction.

37:01.177 --> 37:04.514
And the boss gets demoted
to a regular grunt.

37:06.015 --> 37:08.518
This is beyond pathetic!

37:13.106 --> 37:14.566
He's still Kondo,

37:14.649 --> 37:16.526
whether he's the Commander
or not.

37:19.112 --> 37:20.238
I'm sorry.

37:21.990 --> 37:23.533
Don't get all worked up, Soji.

37:24.284 --> 37:25.493
It's not like you.

37:28.413 --> 37:32.625
Besides, I don't exactly hate
that it's just us now.

37:32.709 --> 37:35.503
It's like being
back in the Shieikan dojo.

37:37.088 --> 37:38.506
[sighs]

37:44.220 --> 37:46.014
[Shimada]
One more round, please.

37:46.055 --> 37:48.475
No! I don't want to anymore!

38:03.239 --> 38:05.408
You didn't eat again?

38:13.750 --> 38:16.669
[♪♪♪]

38:22.300 --> 38:23.760
[sighs]

38:32.393 --> 38:34.479
[Kondo]
Shinpachi's not eating?

38:45.198 --> 38:48.535
The boss even got on his hands
and knees to save his life.

38:50.411 --> 38:53.414
Does he even understand that?

38:53.498 --> 38:55.375
Now, now, don't be
so hard on him.

38:56.334 --> 38:57.794
If I can save all of you

38:59.295 --> 39:02.465
by bowing my head to the ground

39:03.800 --> 39:05.802
then I'll gladly grovel
in the dirt all day long.

39:07.345 --> 39:08.596
Cut the noble act.

39:11.307 --> 39:13.977
That might be fine for you

39:14.060 --> 39:17.146
but when our commander,
Kondo Isami, bows his head

39:17.230 --> 39:20.525
it's the same as making
all of us grovel on the ground.

39:22.986 --> 39:24.445
I'm sorry, Toshi.

39:25.655 --> 39:26.656
But...

39:28.283 --> 39:29.826
I feel for Shinpachi.

39:33.288 --> 39:34.789
He couldn't protect Aijiro.

39:36.666 --> 39:39.669
I feel like
he's punishing himself for it.

39:39.752 --> 39:43.089
But we can't
just let this go on!

39:48.428 --> 39:49.888
Hey, Yamanami.

39:51.472 --> 39:53.099
Can't you do
something?!

39:55.018 --> 39:56.769
I'm at
my breaking point.

39:56.853 --> 39:57.770
Hijikata.

40:02.358 --> 40:03.943
I feel the same way.

40:08.364 --> 40:11.492
[shuffling footsteps
approaching]

40:16.372 --> 40:17.498
[Hijikata]
Kanbei.

40:22.712 --> 40:24.547
I need to have a word with you.

40:25.673 --> 40:27.800
[indistinct shouting]

40:33.723 --> 40:35.725
As fired up as ever, I see.

40:37.060 --> 40:38.895
Hijikata. Haven't you heard?

40:40.188 --> 40:41.522
An imperial edict is out.

40:41.606 --> 40:44.067
The Emperor will personally
expel the foreigners.

40:45.234 --> 40:46.194
An imperial edict?

40:47.779 --> 40:49.530
[Yamanami]
Does that mean
that the Imperial Court

40:49.572 --> 40:51.449
is moving to overthrow
the shogunate?

40:53.034 --> 40:55.787
[Hijikata]
So that's why you're all
so on edge.

40:55.870 --> 40:58.748
[Sagawa]
That would plunge Kyo
into chaos once more.

40:58.831 --> 41:02.210
Now, more than ever,
we need the Mibu Roshigumi.

41:02.293 --> 41:06.422
But for a matter
of such importance...

41:06.506 --> 41:08.424
Serizawa
is our head commander.

41:08.508 --> 41:09.884
Head commander!

41:11.094 --> 41:14.097
This man, Serizawa...
is he truly up to the task?

41:15.974 --> 41:19.185
He extorts "donations"
from everyone...

41:19.268 --> 41:20.603
and I hear he even burned down

41:20.687 --> 41:22.563
a silk wholesaler's shop
recently.

41:25.608 --> 41:30.738
Kondo! Yamanami! Hijikata!
What's the matter with you!

41:31.739 --> 41:33.282
He extorts "donations"
from everyone.

41:33.366 --> 41:34.409
Pathetic! Utterly pathetic!

41:34.492 --> 41:35.535
You think I don't know that?!

41:35.618 --> 41:36.911
Don't get cocky with me!

41:39.998 --> 41:42.166
Where has
your samurai spirit gone?

41:45.503 --> 41:47.463
If you let him run wild,

41:47.547 --> 41:50.258
you'll bring shame
on Lord Katamori.

41:50.341 --> 41:53.219
[Matsudaira]
I don't give a damn
about my reputation

41:53.302 --> 41:54.220
My lord!

42:00.226 --> 42:02.103
Don't you dare hold back!

42:02.145 --> 42:03.271
[all]
Sir!

42:03.354 --> 42:04.397
Let's practice!

42:04.480 --> 42:06.441
[all shouting]

42:06.524 --> 42:07.775
Kanbei.

42:07.817 --> 42:09.277
Yes, sir!

42:09.318 --> 42:15.283
I couldn't care less about the
Mibu-Roshi's internal squabbles.

42:15.324 --> 42:16.534
However...

42:16.617 --> 42:17.869
the edict
about the Emperor himself

42:17.952 --> 42:19.287
leading the overthrow
of the shogunate.

42:21.539 --> 42:23.291
It's a forgery.

42:23.332 --> 42:24.876
[Sagawa]
A forgery?

42:27.170 --> 42:31.966
Choshu plans to use
a forged edict to win allies

42:33.009 --> 42:35.762
and pick a fight
with the shogunate.

42:38.222 --> 42:39.474
Those bastards... playing dirty.

42:39.557 --> 42:41.559
Playing dirty?
There's no such thing.

42:43.561 --> 42:45.146
This is war.

42:54.781 --> 42:56.949
[Serizawa clears throat]

42:57.033 --> 42:58.242
Serizawa!

43:00.620 --> 43:02.330
Well now,
sorry to crash the party.

43:02.413 --> 43:04.457
[Aizu retainer]
Hey! You're in the lord's
presence! Stand back!

43:04.540 --> 43:05.750
Move.

43:07.668 --> 43:11.172
Hey, hey,
what the hell's going on?

43:11.255 --> 43:13.382
I'm just saying I have something
to tell the boss.

43:13.466 --> 43:16.344
And you're the ones making
all this damn noise, aren't you?

43:16.385 --> 43:17.804
Huh? What's the deal?

43:17.887 --> 43:19.138
[Matsudaira]
Kamo!

43:21.057 --> 43:22.892
What is it you wanted
to discuss?

43:24.352 --> 43:27.522
Ah... Our very own Niimi
is connected with Choshu.

43:27.605 --> 43:31.818
[♪♪♪]

43:31.901 --> 43:33.611
You bastard!
What the hell are you saying?!

43:33.694 --> 43:36.072
I found this
in Niimi's letterbox.

43:43.871 --> 43:46.916
It's a letter from Kusaka Genzui
of Choshu, addressed to Niimi.

43:46.999 --> 43:48.960
[Serizawa]
It's all written right there.

43:49.043 --> 43:53.047
Saeki Matasaburo is a Choshu
assassin, hired by Niimi.

43:53.089 --> 43:55.758
Saeki is an assassin?
[Serizawa] Yes.

43:56.634 --> 43:57.760
Then...

44:00.263 --> 44:01.430
The whole thing with Aijiro...

44:01.514 --> 44:03.266
Niimi and Choshu
were behind that, too.

44:07.270 --> 44:08.521
Originally, Kondo...

44:08.604 --> 44:09.772
KONDO

44:10.898 --> 44:13.276
...it seems the plan was
to get rid of you.

44:16.904 --> 44:19.740
Ah, right, and by the way...

44:19.824 --> 44:24.787
Niimi killed Abiru Eisaburo too.

44:27.665 --> 44:29.917
So it's revenge for Abiru.

44:34.672 --> 44:35.798
[Matsudaira]
So?

44:38.926 --> 44:41.804
What are you going to do
about Niimi?

44:41.888 --> 44:43.222
Mm... Not a damn thing.

44:43.306 --> 44:45.391
I knew all along
and didn't do anything.

44:46.976 --> 44:49.270
The man's been far too useful
to me.

44:49.353 --> 44:53.566
If that's true, then you're
subject to punishment as well.

44:53.649 --> 44:54.650
I don't care.

44:54.734 --> 44:56.277
My Lord...

44:56.319 --> 44:59.322
This isn't just an internal
squabble between Mibu factions.

44:59.405 --> 45:03.618
I won't let this man
get away with this. Serizawa!

45:03.659 --> 45:04.994
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

45:05.077 --> 45:06.996
I'll cut you down
right here and now.

45:10.291 --> 45:14.795
Yes! Finally took the bait.

45:14.879 --> 45:19.592
Hey Sagawa, don't chicken out
like last time.

45:19.675 --> 45:23.179
[♪♪♪]

45:24.263 --> 45:25.514
Oh...

45:27.183 --> 45:31.354
If you wanna kill me, you better
come at me with all you've got.

45:33.231 --> 45:34.148
Hey, hey.

45:34.232 --> 45:35.650
[Sagawa]
What do you think you're doing?

45:35.691 --> 45:37.276
[chuckles]

45:38.736 --> 45:41.989
Sorry. This one's my fight.

45:42.031 --> 45:44.867
Oh? Gotten a little stronger,
have we?

45:47.870 --> 45:49.455
[both chuckle]

45:51.540 --> 45:55.878
[Yoshiaki Dewa's "Chiruran
Shinsengumi Requiem" playing]
